    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d250">

                <pb facs="0400" n="288" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg288"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.9315 Manchuria/2: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-07-02T16:00:00+03:00">July 2, 1935—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 2—11:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>261. My 259 and 260 of July 2nd.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d250-f1"/> The Soviet
                    Government is apprehensive that the succession of incidents on the
                    Soviet-Manchurian <pb facs="0401" n="289" xml:id="pg289"/> frontier presages a
                    demand from Japan for demilitarization of border zone and the sale of the
                    northern half of Sakhalin Island.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
